        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Done. Tmux stays; everything is faster, smaller, and quoted. Live sessions (`Downloads`, `environment`) were never touched — all tests ran on scratch sockets, now cleaned up.\n\n## Current workflow (what I found)\n\n- `prefix+f` → popup `tmux-sessionizer`, `prefix+a` → popup `tmux-list`, `prefix+i` → window `tmux-cht.sh`, `prefix+g` → popup `open-repos`. Nvim `C-f` used `neww` sessionizer; zsh `^f`/`^a` run the scripts directly.\n- Sessionizer: fzf over a 10-root `find` → session per basename → windows `1` (shell + typed `nvim`), `2` (shell), `69` (`opencode .` typed), attach/switch. Detection via `pgrep tmux` + `list-sessions | grep`. Hook support via unquoted `send-keys \"source …\"` into the nvim pane (arguably mis-targeted).\n- No other script references window `69`; nothing depends on it. `fd` is installed (`/usr/bin/fd`) and already a documented dependency. TPM + `tmux-sensible` are in use.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- `home/scripts/tmux-sessionizer` — rewrite: `has-session`, direct `new-session -d -s … -n nvim -c … 'nvim'` + named `shell`/`opencode` windows (3 tmux calls vs 7), no `pgrep`/`grep`, fd-first discovery with `find` fallback, missing roots skipped, `sort -u`, full quoting (spaces safe), `:` also sanitized in session names, race-safe create-or-switch, hook sourced into `shell` window with `%q` quoting, `exec` on attach.\n- `home/scripts/tmux-list` — clean no-server message + exit 0, fzf-cancel safe, `exec` attach, full quoting.\n- `home/scripts/tmux-cht.sh` — single `new-window -n 'cht.sh:<topic>'` with POSIX-safe URL quoting (no `bash -c` wrapper), `grep -F` exact matching, no `echo|grep|awk` pipelines.\n- `home/scripts/open-repos` — `git remote -v|grep|awk` → one `awk`; `wc -l` → `mapfile`; URL now from `git remote get-url <name>` so remotes with spaces resolve correctly (was silently truncated). Browser/popup logic untouched.\n- `home/.config/tmux/tmux.conf` — removed dead duplicate `status-style`; `prefix+i` goes straight to `new-window` (no `run-shell` + nested client). TPM/sensible kept.\n- `home/.config/hypr/bindings.{conf,lua}` — launcher is now `exec tmux new-session -A -s Work` (one invocation, attaches to *Work* specifically instead of most-recent session, no lingering bash).\n- `home/.config/nvim/lua/lostheaven/remap.lua` — `C-f` now uses the same `display-popup` sessionizer as `prefix+f`.\n\n## Behavior changes to know\n\n- Session windows are `nvim`/`shell`/`opencode`, not `1`/`2`/`69`. Quitting nvim closes that window (old: fell back to shell) — standard sessionizer behavior.\n- `.tmux-sessionizer` hooks now run in the `shell` window, not typed into nvim.\n- Session names additionally map `:` → `_` (old names with `:` were broken anyway).\n- `prefix+f` was already a popup in your working tree; nvim now matches it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `bash -n` clean on all four scripts; `tmux.conf` loads clean on an isolated socket (`cfg-ok`, prefix `C-f`).\n- Tested on scratch sockets: spaced/dotted/colon paths, hook execution, idempotent re-run (no dup windows), fd + find-fallback + no-finder paths, list attach/switch branching, cht quoting with `'&;` chars, open-repos URL + Zen launch line. Attach \"failures\" in logs are headless-test artifacts (`not a terminal`), same for the old code.\n- Benchmark (warm server, interleaved, `sleep` pane placeholder): old 46/100/247/383 ms vs new 25/61/137/150 ms per session creation — ~2× faster creation; single round-trip ≈ 4 ms, and creation dropped from 7 tmux calls + `pgrep` + `grep` pipeline to 3 + 1. Honest caveat: absolutes inflate as the server accumulates sessions, and discovery/attach costs are unchanged — the win is fewer round-trips and no wasted processes, not magic.\n\nPre-existing working-tree edits I didn't touch (`hyprland.lua` DaVinci rules, `mise/config.toml`, `.zshrc` trylle bits) are still as you left them.",
